      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,P∨(Q∧¬(P∧¬Q))\\,$ | $\\,P∨Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-1}} | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-3}} |\n\nUsing your results, complete the following statement:\n\n$$\nP∨(Q∧¬(P∧¬Q)){{field-4}}P∨Q\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $P≡\\text{T}$ and $Q≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∨(Q∧¬(P∧¬Q)) & ≡\\text{T}∨(\\text{F}∧¬(\\text{T}∧¬\\text{F})) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∨(\\text{F}∧¬(\\text{T}∧\\text{T})) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∨(\\text{F}∧¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∨(\\text{F}∧\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∨\\text{ }\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P≡\\text{F}$ and $Q≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∨Q & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P≡\\text{F}$ and $Q≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∨Q & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.  \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,P∨(Q∧¬(P∧¬Q))\\,$ | $\\,P∨Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $P∨(Q∧¬(P∧¬Q))$ is logically equivalent to $P∨Q,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\text{T},\\text{T},\\text{T},\\text{F}).$ Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\nP∨(Q∧¬(P∧¬Q))≡P∨Q.\n$$",
